---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import CloudIpLookup from '@/components/tools/reference/CloudIpLookup.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="cloud-ip-lookup">
  <CloudIpLookup client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How the cloud IP lookup works</h2>
    <p>
      Large cloud and CDN providers publish the IP ranges they use, so that their customers can write
      firewall rules. The cloud IP lookup combines those lists and finds the entries that contain an
      address or the start of a CIDR range. Each entry has the provider, the service (for example EC2,
      CloudFront or Azure Front Door) and the region when the provider gives one.
    </p>
    <p>
      The lists overlap: a provider can publish a block for a whole region and smaller blocks for
      services inside it. The site merges the lists into ranges that do not overlap, each with every
      entry that covers it, and the page searches them with a binary search after it loads one small
      file.
    </p>
    <h2>When an address is not found</h2>
    <p>
      Not every host publishes its ranges, and a customer can bring its own addresses to a cloud. Use the
      <a href="/ip-address-lookup">IP address lookup</a> to find the network (ASN) that announces any
      address.
    </p>
    <h2>Update schedule</h2>
    <p>
      The lists change often as providers add capacity. The site downloads all of them each week and
      keeps the previous version when a list fails a check.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
